tegy supplementary  planning document can be viewed online  just search playing pitch strategy at  WWF a govt UK paper copies can be made  available on  quest for further details please contact  the planning policy team on 0 1 702 318  191 or planning dot policy at Rochford  gulf qk benefit overpayment help if  you've received letters from the council  about an overpayment of Housing Benefit  or council tax benefit and you're  finding it difficult to pay this amount  back you can contact our revenues &amp;  Benefits Office for help and advice you  can phone us on 0 1 702 318 0 1 1 e-mail  revenues and benefits at Rochford garvey  UK or you can visit the council offices  at South Street Rochford our officers  will be able to answer questions you  have about overpayments and they'll be  able to discuss a suitable arrangement  for you to repay the amount in  affordable instalments independent  advice on overpayments is also available  from the Citizens Advice Bureau many  people who have overpayments of housing  benefit or council tax benefit sometimes  experience difficulty paying other  outstanding debts and household expenses  if this is happening to you then you can  contact or visit your local CA B for  free and independent advice you can  contact them by phoning 0844 for double  7 08 08 visiting their website at www k  or visit their local offices at back  lane rochford or Civic sweet hockley  road Raley the CA B may be able to  negotiate with creditors on your behalf  you can reduce overpayments of Housing  Benefit or council tax benefit by  telling us about changes in your  circumstances as soon as they happen you  can do this by phoning 0170 2318 197 or  318 198 or email revenues and been  it's at Rochford gávea dr. UK or you can  visit the council offices at South  Street Rochford winners of the prize  draw in our last edition of Rochford  district matters we asked customers to  sign up to our council tax paperless  billing scheme to help cut costs and  protect the environment we would like to  thank the hundreds of customers who  responded to the campaign and signed up  to receive their future bills by email  all were entered into a prize draw to  win one of three 100-pound prizes  congratulations to the winners who were  mr Young from Rochford mr. Weldon from  rayleigh and mr. Dawson from rayleigh  the revenues and benefits team are  responsible for producing printing and  posting thousands of bills and booklets  every year by signing up to get your  future bills by email you will help us  to reduce costs and our carbon footprint  paperless billing is convenient for you  convenient for us and very good for the  environment if you would like to receive  your future bills by email let us know  by emailing your name and address to  paperless billing at Rochford garvey you  k and we will do the rest for you the  revenues and benefits team has announced  their performance figures for 2011-12  despite an increasing workload the  department's performance has exceeded  their targets for the first time the  figures show how well the team have been  doing the latest figures come just a few  months after the team gained the  customer service excellence award for  the second year running the award  recognizes their efforts to continually  improve and develop their service in  response to the needs of its customers  the benefits performance figures are  target's for processing benefit claims  21 days performance was nineteen point  four days target for possess processing  change of circumstances was 12 days and  the performance was eight point six days  you can find the revenues and benefits  team on 0 1 702 31 8 197 or 0 1 702 318  198 or email revenues and benefits at  Rochford gulf qk or visit the council  offices at South Street Rochford  neighbourhood policing and the delivery  of local policing services is a core  part of blueprint the new policing model  introduced by essex police earlier this  year dedicated neighborhood constables  will continue to take the lead for  community engagement within their area  and will work with partner agencies to  find solutions to community issues  supported by neighborhood police  community support officers they will  attend neighborhood meetings and will be  the identified points of contact for  their community will now give you names  and mobile phone numbers of the officers  in your area ashington canoe 'don and  Wakering is PC Steve Thomas his mobile  number is 0 7 80 1 4616 534 hullbridge  is pc emma chambers mobile 078 1395 3703  Rochford is pc paul ledger mobile number  0 7 8 0 1 4616 53 hockley is pc charles  key mobile 077 100 4 6-1 6-1 and in  rayleigh it's PC Steve joins mobile Oh  seven eight one two three nine five  three seven zero three and you can find  out more about neighbourhood policing  and the work Essex Police do at ww Essex  Police UK winners of hate crime logo  competition pupils from Fitz why mark  school rayleigh led the way in a logo  design competition to draw attention to  the help available for victims of hate  crime charity Wilkins katie orchard and  holly Perkins  took the top three places in the  competition organized by Rochford  district hate crime panel and supported  by the Rochford District Community  Safety Partnership the panel has been  set up to promote awareness of hate  crime and works with many different  organizations and community groups to  change people's attitude to others the  logo competition was designed to  encourage young people to think about  hate crime and how victims might be  encouraged to come forward and report  incidents charities winning entry won  her a 50 pounds amazon voucher Katie and  Holly collected a 25 pound voucher and a  10 pound voucher respectively and were  presented with their prizes by the chair  of the hate crime panel Paul Becker's  and the chair of the Oxford District  Community Safety Partnership counselor  Joe McPherson during a school assembly  unfortunately charity was unable to be  at the presentation but received her  reward later Park events success scores  of dog owners and cyclists took  advantage of a free microchipping  service as part of a series of events  held in parks and open spaces across the  district the four events in Great  Wakering Cherry Orchard country park  rochford and rayleigh saw more than 40  dogs fitted with microchips to help  identify them should they ever go astray  the free bike taking service proved just  as popular with 50 bicycles being fitted  over the four events all those who  completed an on-site survey were entered  into a prize draw with a 15 pounds Marks  and Spencers voucher as prizes the  winning visitors were from Great  Wakering miss MERS H Mitchell of great  wakering Cherry Orchard was mrs. our  tents le of Rayleigh Rochford MERS tea  green of Rochford and freely mrs. K  baglietto  rochford district matters is edited by  patrick john and produced by rockford  district council who can be found at  three to nineteen south street rochford  SS for one BW their telephone number is  0 1 702 546 366 and their website is at  WWE r govt UK the paper is printed by  Charmin &amp; Company Limited and that  brings us to the end of a situation  which was recorded by volunteers from  the rayleigh Rockford and castle point  talking newspapers for the blind at  their studio in rockford
 

